# A chain through in gets a general help.
mode: syntax
---- query
t | where a in (1) == true
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..27
  PIPELINE@0..26
    NAME_REF@0..1
      IDENT@0..1 "t"
    WHITESPACE@1..2 " "
    PIPE@2..3 "|"
    WHITESPACE@3..4 " "
    WHERE_OP@4..26
      IDENT@4..9 "where"
      WHITESPACE@9..10 " "
      BIN_EXPR@10..26
        IN_EXPR@10..18
          NAME_REF@10..11
            IDENT@10..11 "a"
          WHITESPACE@11..12 " "
          IDENT@12..14 "in"
          WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
          ARG_LIST@15..18
            L_PAREN@15..16 "("
            LITERAL@16..17
              LONG@16..17 "1"
            R_PAREN@17..18 ")"
        WHITESPACE@18..19 " "
        EQ2@19..21 "=="
        WHITESPACE@21..22 " "
        LITERAL@22..26
          TRUE_KW@22..26 "true"
  WHITESPACE@26..27 "\n"

error[DS0101]: comparison operators cannot be chained
  --> query:1:20
  |
1 | t | where a in (1) == true
  |           -------- ^^ a second comparison
  |           |
  |           the result of this comparison is not a value to compare again
  |
  = help: compare each pair separately and combine them with `and`
